From 96daef5271ae6f7d3148eea8f8fd1bfdf2b83e38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 18:57:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Scope telematics down to trip/km/time/location; drop Damoov
 and harsh-driving detection
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Removes harsh-braking/acceleration/cornering/speeding detection and the
GPS-only crash heuristic from autoTripEngine, along with the crash-alert
push notification pipeline and the never-activated Damoov SDK integration.
Trip start/stop detection, distance/duration integration, live location,
and trip history are untouched — they never depended on any of this.

- autoTripEngine/autoTripStorage: remove detectDrivingEvents, the crash
  heuristic, and the state fields that only existed to support them
- Delete crashAlert.ts, useCrashAlert.ts, CrashAlertModal.tsx (and its
  mount in the driver tab layout)
- Delete useDamoovTelemetry.ts, damoov/telematicsSdk.ts,
  withDamoovManifest.js, and the Damoov Maven repo / react-native-telematics
  dependency
- useDrivingSafety/DrivingSafetyCard: keep only the trip-metrics half
  (distance, trips, driving time, idle time, speed, night/weekend trips),
  drop the safety score, event counts, and coaching tips
- Backend: unschedule weekly-safety-trust-score and drop
  award_weekly_safety_trust_points() (its only data source, driving_events,
  is gone — leaving it running would have silently awarded every driver a
  flat weekly trust bonus once event counts were permanently zero), drop
  driving_events and the four empty Damoov telematics tables, drop
  cars.damoov_vehicle_token
